 China Press and Springer-Verlag Berlin Heidelberg 2014 math.scichina.com link.springer.com\n\nSome classes of complete permutation\n\npolynomials over F q\n\nWU GaoFei 1, LI Nian 2, HELLESETH Tor 3& ZHANG YuQing 1,4,∗\n\n1 State Key Laboratory of Integrated Service Networks, Xidian University, Xi’an 710071,China;\n\n2 Information Security and National Computing Grid Laboratory,\n\nSouthwest Jiaotong University, Chengdu 610031,China;\n\n3 Department of Informatics, University of Bergen, Bergen N-5020,Norway;\n\n4 National Computer Network Intrusion Protection Center,\n\nUniversity of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing 100043,China\n\nEmail: wugf@nipc.org.cn, nianli.2010@gmail.com, Tor.Helleseth@ii.uib.no, zhangyq@ucas.ac.cn\n\nReceived June 9, 2014; accepted September 12, 2014; published online December 30, 2014\n\nAbstract By using a powerful criterion for permutation polynomials, we give several classes of complete per-\n\nmutation polynomials over ﬁnite ﬁelds. First, two classes of complete permutation monomials whose exponents\n\nare of Niho type are presented. Second, for any odd prime p, we give a suﬃcient and necessary condition for\n\na−1 x d to be a complete permutation polynomial over F p 4 k,where d=p 4 k−1\n\np k−1+1 and a∈F∗\n\np 4 k.Finally, we\n\npresent a class of complete permutation multinomials, which is a generalization of recent work.\n\nKeywords ﬁnite ﬁeld, complete permutation polynomials, Walsh transform, Niho exponents, Dickson poly-\n\nnomials\n\nMSC(2010) 05A05, 11T06\n\nCitation: Wu G F, Li N, Helleseth T, et al. Some classes of complete permutation polynomials over F q.SciChina\n\nMath, 2015, 58: 2081–2094, doi: 10.1007/s11425-014-4964-2\n\n1 Introduction\n\nLet p be a prime and n be a positive integer. Let F q be a ﬁnite ﬁeld of q=p n elements. We denote\n\nby F∗\n\nq the multiplicative group of F q.Apolynomial f∈F q[x] is called a permutation polynomial (PP)\n\nif the associated polynomial mapping f:c→ f(c)from F q to itself is a permutation of F q(see [8]).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFurther results on complete permutation monomials over finite fields (https://doi.org/10.1016%2Fj.ffa.2019.01.003)\nciteturn1search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Furthermore, the authors wrote “As a corollary, a conjecture by Wu, Li, Helleseth and Zhang is proven in odd characteristic”. ... Then we derive two new classes of complete permutation monomials of {\\mathbb{F}}_{{q}^{n}} for general n such that or respectively (see Theorem 5 and Theorem 6).\n## Conjecture 4.18 in [42]\n\nLet be a prime such that . Let and , and . Then there exists such that is a Dickson polynomial of degree over {\\mathbb{F}}_{{p}^{k}}.\n\nUsing the classification of exceptional polynomials, Bartoli et al. [8] classified complete permutation monomials of degree over {\\mathbb{F}}_{{q}^{n}}, where q is odd, is prime and . Furthermore, the authors wrote “As a corollary, a conjecture by Wu, Li, Helleseth and Zhang is proven in odd characteristic”. However, their result on Conjecture 1 were not given in explicit format; see Proposition 3.4 in [8].\n\nOn the other hand, the second conjecture (Conjecture 4.20 in [42]) was proven recently in [24].\n\nTheorem 1\n\n## Theorem 3.2 in [24]\n\nLet p be an odd prime. Let and . Then is a CPP over {\\mathbb{F}}_{{p}^{nk}}, where such that .\n\nWe note that this result is true for prime . However, when is large or not prime, the classification of CPP exponents is still open. For example, when is a power of primes such as 8 or 9, only a few new examples of CPPs are provided in [8]. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThis page intentionally left blank (https://www.nzdr.ru/data/media/biblio/kolxoz/Cs/CsCr/Blahut%20R.E.%20Algebraic%20Codes%20on%20Lines%2C%20Planes%2C%20and%20Curves%20%28CUP%2C%202008%29%28ISBN%200521771943%29%28567s%29_CsCr_.pdf)\nciteturn1search12 [wordlim: 200] Publishe