nArticle\n\n  * Jun 2023\n\n  * Gaofei Wu\n  * Keqin Feng\n  * Nian Li\n  * Tor Helleseth\n\nThe cross-correlation between two maximum length sequences ( m -sequences) of the same period has been studied since the end of 1960s. One open conjecture by Helleseth states that the cross-correlation between any two p -ary m -sequences takes on the value –1 for at least one shift provided that the decimation d obeys d ≡ 1 (mod p – 1). This was known as the –1 conjecture. Up to now, the –1 conjecture was confirmed for the following decimations: (1) Niho-type decimations, i.e., d = s ( p ^{ n /2} – 1) + 1, where s is an integer; (2) all the complete permutation polynomial (CPP) exponents d satisfying d ≡ 1 (mod p –1); and (3) the additional families of decimations tabulated in this paper. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTor Helleseth | UiB (https://www4.uib.no/finn-ansatte/tor.helleseth)\nciteturn1search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Constructions of complete permutation polynomials. (ekstern lenke) ...   * Ziran Tu; Xiangyong Zeng; Tor Helleseth (2018). ...   * Zhengchun Zhou; Tor Helleseth; Udaya Parampalli (2018).\n  * Guang Gong; Tor Helleseth; P. Vijay Kumar (2018). Solomon W. Golomb - Mathematician, Engineer, and Pioneer. (ekstern lenke)\n  * Xiaofang Xu; Chunlei Li; Xiangyong Zeng et al. (2018). Constructions of complete permutation polynomials. (ekstern lenke)\n  * Ziran Tu; Xiangyong Zeng; Chunlei Li et al. (2018). A class of new permutation trinomials. (ekstern lenke)\n  * Ziran Tu; Xiangyong Zeng; Tor Helleseth (2018). New permutation quadrinomials over F22m. (ekstern lenke)\n  * Zhengchun Zhou; Tor Helleseth; Udaya Parampalli (2018). A Family of Polyphase Sequences with Asymptotically Optimal Correlation. (ekstern lenke)\n  * Ziran Tu; Xiangyong Zeng; Tor Helleseth (2018). A class of permutation quadrinomials. (ekstern lenke)\n  * Vladimir Edemskiy; Chunlei Li; Xiangyong Zeng et al. (2018). The linear c